  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...A marginal risk for severe storms and a slight\nrisk of enhanced rainfall remains for portions of the area this\nafternoon into this evening.\n\nA cold front will continue to move across the area this\nafternoon into this evening and overnight. Ahead of the cold\nfront, warm/humid air will remain in place across eastern New\nJersey, as well as central/southern Delaware and eastern\nMaryland, leading to CAPE values of 1000-2000 J/kg. As a mid- \nlevel/ short wave/vorticity impulse moves across the area this \nafternoon into tonight, showers and thunderstorms should \ndevelop across the area. With 1000-2000 J/kg of CAPE, along with\nshear values near 30-40 knots, a few strong to severe storms \nmay develop across portions of eastern New Jersey, as well as \ncentral/southern Delaware and eastern Maryland. With PW values \nin the 1.5-2.0 range, heavy rainfall will also remain possible.\n\nAfter tonight, the front will shift offshore, bringing the rain\nwith it. As high pressure builds in from the north, dry weather\nwill return through the much of the weekend.",
